    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine is anchored today by **Luis Robert Jr.**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 77.40. Facing Bennett and his 3.99 xERA, **Luis Robert Jr.** benefits immensely from a favorable park environment and a dynamic platoon advantage that boosts his output potential significantly. Furthermore, the slow delivery profile of the opposing starter provides an elite opportunity for stolen base production, a critical needle-mover in our 5x5 Roto context. **Kyle Tucker** (65.64) and **Coby Mayo** (65.57) also provide high-end production; **Coby Mayo** specifically capitalizes on a massive 16% park adjustment against Bennett, while **Kyle Tucker** maintains strong core value despite the uncertainty of his pending lineup spot.\n\nRounding out the core, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (64.99) remains a high-floor play against Bibee, leveraging a solid SP skill matchup to overcome a minor platoon hurdle. **Gunnar Henderson** (62.67) and **Sam Antonacci** (61.20) round out our recommended starts, both benefiting from high-leverage spots in their respective batting orders. **Miguel Vargas** serves as our final starter at 52.92; while his projection is more marginal, his xwOBA of .389 against Brown, H makes him a reliable plug-in compared to the current void on our bench. With **Jackson Merrill**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Andy Pages** all unavailable due to scheduling or injury, the optimizer faced minimal friction today, essentially clearing the path for our top-tier talent to shoulder the load without competition from depth options like **Jacob Wilson** or **Heliot Ramos**. Owners should monitor the official lineup for **Kyle Tucker** closely, as any move out of the top six could dampen his efficiency, but current data suggests a strong night ahead for the Waves.",
